  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>For the given process&nbsp;pressure is constant therefore, it is an isobaric process.</p><p>For a quasi-static process the change in internal energy of an ideal gas is independent of the nature of the process and is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p>[molar heat capacity at constant volume for monatomic gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>]</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3486</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
